Hairy Dragon wrote:
> If I were to start playing rogue-like games, which game is most recommended? 

Since you're asking here in this group, Nethack is the answer. :-)

More seriously... Yes, indeed, Nethack is one of the two I like most.
The other one is Slash'em. Nethack is IMO better balanced and has not
such fancy stuff in it as Slash'em. The latter has much more options,
objects, monsters, races, levels; I think it is significantly harder.

If you want to start, as you say, I'd choose Nethack. Then play until
you think you don't progress any more. Ask here for advice and continue
Nethack. If you then feel getting better in Nethack and know the basic
tactics and some survival strategies have a look at Slash'em.

Don't ask me to explain why I suggest so complicated a process.

If you want a simple answer that would be just Nethack.

Okay, you may first want to play the origin of all reguelikes, Rogue,
that is a lot simpler. But no, better play Nethack; it's the best.

